WEBVTT

00:08:30.339 --> 00:08:32.925
And hopefully, it's becoming
increasingly clear

00:08:32.967 --> 00:08:35.761
that this isn't
just an astrophysics problem

00:08:35.761 --> 00:08:38.722
of galaxies and galaxy clusters,

00:08:38.764 --> 00:08:41.850
but this is also
a particle physics problem.

00:08:41.892 --> 00:08:46.397
In order to understand
what's happening on the largest scales,

00:08:46.438 --> 00:08:49.024
we need to understand
something very small,

00:08:49.066 --> 00:08:50.734
like a new particle,

00:08:50.734 --> 00:08:52.736
or maybe primordial black holes.

00:08:54.154 --> 00:08:56.282
So you've been looking
at this for a moment,

00:08:56.282 --> 00:08:58.784
and you know what you're all
really thinking is,

00:08:58.826 --> 00:09:01.120
"What's Chanda's favorite
dark matter candidate?"